+# SH-0007 Consolidated Restaurant RC1 Offline Acceptance — beta.58.31
+
+Candidate: `10.5.4-beta.58.31`
+Device: SH-0007 only.
+Production SH-0005 / SH-0006: do not touch.
+Canonical Stock: OFF. Cutover: OFF.
+Preserve Seq293 / Seq304 / Seq316; never Retry/Delete/Reset them.
+
+Run this as one consolidated practical session after the approved x64 installer is installed once.
+
+1. Confirm the installed version is `10.5.4-beta.58.31` and Business/Branch are the isolated Beta test context.
+2. Confirm no unexpected Offline Conflict/DLQ cleanup occurred before testing.
+3. Go Offline. Open a shift, create Sale A, create an Expense, create Sale B, close/reopen app where the scenario requires it, and verify the local read models remain visible.
+4. Create a Customer Offline, then create a Sale for that Customer before reconnect. Verify local success is not shown as `Failed to fetch`.
+5. Create a Delivery order Offline with valid phone/address/zone. Verify missing/invalid phone, address, or wrong-branch zone fail before durable Sale creation.
+6. For an Offline-created Delivery sale, move lifecycle through Preparing -> Ready -> driver assignment -> Delivered before first server ACK. Verify local status/custody projections remain coherent.
+7. Create a Return against a brand-new Offline Sale before that Sale receives its server ACK. Verify the Return stays dependency-gated and later maps to the authoritative server order/item IDs exactly once.
+8. Attempt a second pending Return against the same available quantity before Sync. Verify the locally reserved quantity blocks over-return.
+9. Check driver custody while Offline. Verify pending cash-delivered orders appear from snapshot + local projection. Settlement must remain disabled/Online-only.
+10. Open Inventory while Offline. Verify only the latest complete timestamped snapshot is shown; if no complete snapshot exists, the page fails closed rather than showing fake zeros.
+11. Exercise representative Storage/Admin actions with network unavailable and with DNS/fetch failure. Verify they stop before first upload/write and clearly require Internet.
+12. Create one durable Sale with the printer unavailable. Verify the Sale remains saved once, print failure does not retry/duplicate the Sale, and later reprint does not create another economic Sale.
+13. Reconnect. Force/allow Sync. Verify explicit ACKs, no lost operations, no duplicate economics, no orphan dependencies, and no duplicate Local + Server row for the same `client_tx_id`.
+14. Verify the temporary `OFF-*` local reference is replaced in the reconciled server representation by the server-assigned official bon/invoice number; Offline never guessed the official number.
+15. Verify the Offline-created Customer is linked to the final server Sale after Customer ACK mapping.
+16. Verify the pending-Sale Return resolves to the final server order/item IDs and the return appears exactly once.
+17. Verify delivery custody after reconnect and perform settlement Online only; then verify shift close respects remaining custody.
+18. Cold restart while Offline after local activity and verify supported cached operational pages remain usable with visible Offline/stale semantics.
+19. Recheck Seq293 / Seq304 / Seq316 are unchanged and preserved.
+20. Export one support bundle after the run and keep it with the acceptance record.
+
+Acceptance is PASS only if there are zero duplicate economic operations, zero lost durable operations, zero orphan dependencies, zero unexpected conflicts, and all Online-only actions fail closed before partial mutation.
